        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foresthill%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Jenny Lind mine once yielded about $2,500 of gold a day, totaling over $1 million by 1880.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foresthill%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1868, all Forest Hill mines had produced roughly $10 million, with gold selling for $16 an ounce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foresthill%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Hardy‑Kennedy building, erected 1862, was the first fireproof store in Foresthill and is now the Langstaff building still in use.",
